---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';import '../../../../styles/equipment.css';
const d='/equipment/12-11/',leica='https://downloads.leica-microsystems.com/LMD7/Product%20Configuration%20%26%20Tech%20Specs/Leica_LMD6_7-TechnicalBrochure_en_2022.08.08.pdf',photos='https://www.leica-microsystems.com/products/light-microscopes/p/leica-lmd7/media/';
---
<Layout pageTitle="Leica LMD7 static reference and offline annotation" description="Orbit a dormant Leica LMD7 and use an independent teaching grid to measure an arbitrary polygon area." wide={true}>
<article class="equipment" id="lmd7"><nav class="eq-nav"><a href="/simulations/equipment/12-11/">← Equipment 12-11</a><a href="/simulations/equipment/">Register</a><a href="#lmd-evidence">Evidence</a></nav>
<header class="eq-mast"><p class="eq-meta">12-11 / DORMANT EXTERIOR · INDEPENDENT GEOMETRY</p><h2>Trace a polygon on a separate grid</h2><p class="eq-lede">Inspect the Leica LMD7 scanning-stage exterior. Try the disconnected teaching board beside it to check how an outline's area changes with its vertices.</p></header>
<div class="l-cols"><section><h3>Static Leica exterior</h3><canvas id="lmd-model" aria-label="Orbitable Leica LMD7 shell and separate non-connected board"></canvas><p id="lmd-viewstatus" role="status">Loading metric GLB…</p><button id="lmd-front">Reset overview</button><button id="lmd-side">Stage-side view</button><button id="lmd-board">Offline board view</button></section>
<section><h3>Fictional grid annotation</h3><svg id="lmd-chart" viewBox="0 0 100 70" role="img" aria-label="Independent 100 by 70 annotation grid"><defs><pattern id="lmd-lines" width="10" height="10" patternUnits="userSpaceOnUse"><path d="M10 0H0V10" fill="none" stroke="#648485" stroke-width=".36"/></pattern></defs><rect width="100" height="70" fill="#182c30"/><rect width="100" height="70" fill="url(#lmd-lines)"/><polygon id="lmd-fill" fill="#ddb366" fill-opacity=".35" stroke="#f3bc72" stroke-width=".52"/><polyline id="lmd-edge" fill="none" stroke="#f3bc72" stroke-width=".46"/><g id="lmd-vertices" fill="#e9f5ed"/></svg>
<p id="lmd-area" role="status"></p><p>New polygon clears the example. Tap the grid or add integer points below, then close the outline. Inputs are fictional grid coordinates only.</p>
<div class="l-points"><label>X <input id="lmd-x" type="number" min="0" max="100" value="20"/></label><label>Y <input id="lmd-y" type="number" min="0" max="70" value="15"/></label><button id="lmd-add">Add point</button></div>
<button id="lmd-example">Load example rectangle</button><button id="lmd-clear">New polygon</button><button id="lmd-undo">Undo or reopen</button><button id="lmd-close">Close outline</button><p id="lmd-notice" role="alert"></p><button id="lmd-export">Download area report</button><p><a href={d+'example-area.json'}>Example area report</a>. It contains no vertices, path, calibration or machine coordinates.</p></section></div>
<section id="lmd-evidence"><h3>Configuration and source views</h3><div class="l-cols"><figure><img src={d+'station.webp'} alt="Original front render of the LMD7 with a separate green grid board"/><figcaption>Original front reference. <a href={leica+'#page=1'}>Leica August 2022 technical brochure, cover</a> shows the wide dark scanning stage and upright body. Stand size: 512 × 649.6 × 596.5 mm (W × H × D; scanning-stage version, <a href={leica+'#page=2'}>p. 2</a>).</figcaption></figure><figure><img src={d+'side.webp'} alt="Original stage-side rendering of dormant Leica exterior"/><figcaption>Original alternate view. <a href={photos}>Leica LMD7 manufacturer gallery</a> establishes the dark sleeves, guard silhouette and exterior module. Internal details, housing proportions and capped accessories are inferred; no accessory functionality is modeled.</figcaption></figure></div>
<h3>Geometric check</h3><p>The example area is independently 40 × 25 = 1,000 square grid units. For a general simple polygon the board sums the signed cross products of adjacent vertices, divides by two and takes the absolute value. This computes polygon area, not a raster mask.</p>
<table><thead><tr><th>Check</th><th>Expected</th><th>Actual</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>40 × 25 rectangle</td><td>1,000 grid units²</td><td>1,000 exact</td></tr><tr><td>10 × 10 right triangle</td><td>50 grid units²</td><td>50 exact, both vertex orientations</td></tr><tr><td>Self-crossing outline</td><td>Reject, no result</td><td>Rejected without modifying vertices</td></tr><tr><td>Scan-stage enclosure bounds</td><td>Within 0.5 mm of cited dimensions</td><td>0.5 mm tolerance passed</td></tr></tbody></table>
<p>There is no acquisition, cutting, specimen state, instrument command or hardware transform. The register's area check has an offline analogue; its child-mask and lineage behavior is not implemented.</p><p><a href={d+'build-model.py'}>Editable Blender source</a> · <a href={d+'lmd7.glb'}>Metric GLB</a> · <a href={d+'area-board.mjs'}>Offline solver and schema</a> · <a href={d+'vr.json'}>VR IDs and bounds</a>. No headset verification claimed.</p></section></article></Layout>
<script>import '../../../../lib/equipment/12-11/client.mjs';</script>
<style is:global>
#lmd7 .l-cols{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.15fr) minmax(0,1fr);gap:1rem}#lmd7 section{margin:1rem 0;padding:1rem;border:1px solid var(--border);min-width:0}
#lmd7 :is(button,input){font:inherit;color:inherit;background:var(--panel);border:1px solid var(--border);padding:.4rem;margin:.2rem .2rem .2rem 0;max-width:100%}
#lmd7 button{cursor:pointer}#lmd7 button:disabled{opacity:.55;cursor:default}#lmd7 :is(button,input):focus-visible{outline:2px solid #b28d5e}
#lmd-model{width:100%;height:355px;display:block;touch-action:none}#lmd-chart{display:block;width:min(100%,390px);margin:auto;cursor:crosshair}
#lmd7 .l-points{display:flex;align-items:center;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.35rem}#lmd7 .l-points input{width:4rem}
#lmd7 figure{margin:.5rem 0}#lmd7 figure img{width:100%}
#lmd7 table{width:100%;font-size:.94rem;border-collapse:collapse;text-align:left}#lmd7 td,#lmd7 th{border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);padding:.35rem}
@media(max-width:850px){#lmd7 .l-cols{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr)}#lmd-model{height:282px}#lmd-chart{width:min(88%,360px)}}
</style>
